I need to decide on the materials: a pinkish red jewel and a cyan one would contrast nicely. I'll create two MeshStandardMaterials with appropriate colors, emissive values, metalness, and roughness to give them a subtle glow. Then, within the loop, after creating each spike, I'll also create a small sphere (ball) positioned slightly above the spike tip, and an octahedron (jewel) offset a bit to create a cluster effect. The ball can reuse the base material (so it looks like part of the hat), while the jewel uses the new jewel materials, alternating between the two for variety.

